le.maxHeartbeats false`\n✔ [9250/9250] Built MIPStarRE.QPBT.Extraction.SourceUnitary (8.8s)\nBuild completed successfully (9250 jobs)."}], "initial_body": "### Motivation\n- Address #585. The paper's `lem:qld-unitary` states a fourth-root extraction\n  rate in the same global error family used by `lem:qld-4-7`. The existing\n  composition retained an extra nested construction error. See the paper\n  mirror `14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex`, lines 1664-1685.\n\n### Description\n- Add `exists_extractionWitness_fourth_root_rate`, choosing universal\n  constants internally before the admissible parameters and projective\n  setting. It produces the global witness and extraction witness with error\n  `deltaExtract C (deltaQld ...)`, without the extra nested construction error.\n- Reuse the existing robustness absorption results. Keep the existing\n  constructor, source-domain qualifications and pending isometry/final\n  soundness obligations, and record the new rate in the blueprint and gap note.\n- Publish the completed proof from `9f58154b` after a normal main refresh;\n  the SourceUnitary module is unchanged by the refresh.\n\n### Testing\n- The author passed focused Lean, targeted SourceUnitary/QPBT builds, root\n  import, fresh standard-only axiom closure, declaration resolution,\n  blueprint rendering and normal commit hooks.\n- The author's separate sync check reported 236 stale entries in an ignored\n  generated index; that diagnostic remains recorded. Current canonical\n  publication and exact-head CI are pending and will check the refreshed state.\n- MAIN verified the clean two-parent refresh and byte-identical proof module.\n  Fresh independent review remains required.\n\n---\nAddresses #585\n", "author_evidence": "results/telemetry/native-audits/issue585-unitary-rate-01a0b205/", "claims_held": ["main-update585", "main-update591"]}
